window.__SEARCH_INDEX__=[{"t":"Configuration","p":"Configuration","u":"getting-started/configuration.html","x":"All settings live in site.yml."},{"t":"Navigation","p":"Configuration","u":"getting-started/configuration.html#navigation","x":"The nav key is the layout of your site. Entries are Title: path.md, and a title that maps to a list becomes a collapsible section: nav: - Home: index.md - Getting Started: - Installation: getting-started/installation.md - Configuration: getting-started/configuration.md - Source code: https://github.com # external links work too Paths are relative to docs/. If you leave nav out, it is generated from the folder structure, with index.md first in each folder."},{"t":"Appearance","p":"Configuration","u":"getting-started/configuration.html#appearance","x":"theme: primary: \"#00796b\" # accent color, light mode primary_dark: \"#3ddbc0\" # accent color, dark mode default_mode: auto # auto | light | dark code_light: xcode code_dark: github-dark fonts: true # false = system fonts only, no Google Fonts request logo: assets/logo.svg # optional, shown next to the site name Any Pygments style name works for the code themes. Text on buttons switches between white and near-black automatically so it stays readable on whatever accent you choose."},{"t":"Landing page","p":"Configuration","u":"getting-started/configuration.html#landing-page","x":"Give a page template: home.html and describe its hero and highlights in the front matter. The Markdown below the front matter is shown after the highlights. --- title: Acme Docs template: home.html hero: title: Write Markdown. Get a documentation site. text: One supporting sentence. actions: - {text: Get started, link: getting-started/installation.md, style: primary} - {text: Learn more, link: guide/embedding.md, style: secondary} code_title: site.yml # optional code window beside the headline code_lang: yaml code: | nav: - Home: index.md # image: assets/screenshot.png # use instead of code features: - title: First highlight text: A sentence or two. link: guide/embedding.md wide: true # spans two columns; pair wide cards with normal ones --- The first level of nav also becomes a row of section tabs in the top bar."},{"t":"Page options","p":"Configuration","u":"getting-started/configuration.html#page-options","x":"A page can start with YAML front matter: --- title: Custom title # otherwise the first # heading is used description: Shown in <meta> tags hide_title: true # skip the auto-generated h1 when the page has none search: false # leave this page out of the search index ---"},{"t":"Settings reference","p":"Configuration","u":"getting-started/configuration.html#settings-reference","x":"Key Default Purpose use_directory_urls false true builds page/index.html for clean URLs exclude_docs [] Extra glob patterns to skip (.* and _* always are) extra_css [] Stylesheets to add, relative to docs/ extra_javascript [] Scripts to add, relative to docs/ markdown_extensions [] Extra Python-Markdown extensions Directory URLs and local files With use_directory_urls: true, links end in /, which browsers can't open from disk. Host the site on a web server (or use build.py serve) in that mode. Continue with writing content."},{"t":"Installation","p":"Installation","u":"getting-started/installation.html","x":"You need Python 3.9 or newer. pip install markdown pyyaml jinja2 pygments Then, from the project folder: python build.py build # writes the site to ./site python build.py serve # live preview at http://127.0.0.1:8000"},{"t":"Project layout","p":"Installation","u":"getting-started/installation.html#project-layout","x":"mdsite/ ├── build.py # the generator ├── site.yml # site settings and navigation ├── docs/ # your Markdown files, images and other assets │ ├── index.md │ └── _snippets/ # partials: never published on their own └── theme/ # templates, CSS and JS (the predefined style)"},{"t":"Verify the build","p":"Installation","u":"getting-started/installation.html#verify-the-build","x":"Shared snippet This paragraph lives in _snippets/shared-note.md and is included by more than one page. Edit it once and every page that includes it updates. Next: configure the site."},{"t":"Embeds & includes","p":"Embeds & includes","u":"guide/embedding.html","x":"Directives go on a line of their own. Inside fenced code blocks they are never executed, which is how this page can show you the syntax."},{"t":"Embeds","p":"Embeds & includes","u":"guide/embedding.html#embeds","x":"{% embed \"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jNQXAC9IVRw\" title=\"Me at the zoo\" caption=\"The first YouTube video.\" %} Result: The first YouTube video. The URL decides how it is embedded: URL Rendered as YouTube / youtu.be privacy-friendly YouTube player Vimeo, CodePen their embed players .mp4, .webm, .mov HTML5 video .mp3, .wav, .ogg HTML5 audio .pdf inline PDF viewer local .html or any other https:// <iframe> Options: title, caption, ratio=\"4/3\" and height=\"480\"."},{"t":"A local interactive page","p":"Embeds & includes","u":"guide/embedding.html#a-local-interactive-page","x":"Put the file anywhere in docs/ (here assets/demo.html) and point to it with a relative path: {% embed \"../assets/demo.html\" title=\"Counter demo\" height=\"220\" caption=\"A self-contained HTML file.\" %} A self-contained HTML file."},{"t":"Includes","p":"Embeds & includes","u":"guide/embedding.html#includes","x":"Reuse a Markdown partial in several pages. The path is relative to the current file, or to docs/: {% include \"_snippets/shared-note.md\" %} Shared snippet This paragraph lives in _snippets/shared-note.md and is included by more than one page. Edit it once and every page that includes it updates. The --8<-- \"file\" form used by MkDocs snippets works too."},{"t":"Include source files as code","p":"Embeds & includes","u":"guide/embedding.html#include-source-files-as-code","x":"Any non-Markdown file is inserted as a highlighted code block. Add lines=\"3-8\" to show only part of it: {% include \"_snippets/hello.py\" lines=\"3-8\" %} def add(a: int, b: int) -> int: \"\"\"Add two numbers.\"\"\" return a + b def main() -> None:"},{"t":"Diagrams","p":"Embeds & includes","u":"guide/embedding.html#diagrams","x":"A fenced mermaid block becomes a diagram (the page loads Mermaid from a CDN, so it needs internet access): flowchart LR A[Markdown] --> B(build.py) B --> C[HTML pages] B --> D[Search index]"},{"t":"Writing content","p":"Writing content","u":"guide/writing-content.html","x":"Standard Markdown plus the \"extra\" features: tables, footnotes, definition lists, abbreviations and attribute lists."},{"t":"Admonitions","p":"Writing content","u":"guide/writing-content.html#admonitions","x":"Note A plain note. The title defaults to the type name. Custom title Admonitions can hold formatting, code, and lists: first second Success Something went well. Warning Be careful here. Do not do this Destructive action ahead. ??? example \"Collapsible example\" Use ??? instead of !!! only if you add the pymdownx.details extension."},{"t":"Code","p":"Writing content","u":"guide/writing-content.html#code","x":"Fenced code is highlighted at build time and gets a copy button: def greet(name: str) -> str: \"\"\"Return a friendly greeting.\"\"\" return f\"Hello, {name}!\" print(greet(\"docs\")) Inline code looks like this. Keyboard keys: Ctrl + K."},{"t":"Tables","p":"Writing content","u":"guide/writing-content.html#tables","x":"Column Type Notes id integer Primary key title string Required archived boolean Defaults to false"},{"t":"Lists and definitions","p":"Writing content","u":"guide/writing-content.html#lists-and-definitions","x":"Ordered item Another item nested bullet another one Term Definition of the term, written with a leading colon. The HTML spec is maintained by the W3C and WHATWG."},{"t":"Footnotes","p":"Writing content","u":"guide/writing-content.html#footnotes","x":"Footnotes are collected at the bottom of the page.1"},{"t":"Card grids","p":"Writing content","u":"guide/writing-content.html#card-grids","x":"Wrap a list in a grid cards block to lay it out as cards: <div class=\"grid cards\" markdown=\"1\"> - **Fast builds** Hundreds of pages in a second. - **Plain files** Nothing to install on the server. </div> Fast builds Hundreds of pages in a second. Plain files Nothing to install on the server. Yours to change Edit the theme's CSS and templates."},{"t":"Images and links","p":"Writing content","u":"guide/writing-content.html#images-and-links","x":"Images can be sized with attribute lists: Links to other pages use the file name, so they keep working if you rename the output: back to the start, installation. Like this one. ↩"},{"t":"Quick start","p":"Simulation workshop","u":"index.html#quick-start","x":"pip install markdown pyyaml jinja2 pygments python build.py serve Open http://127.0.0.1:8000. Edit any file in docs/ and the page reloads. When you're ready to publish, run python build.py build and upload the site/ folder."},{"t":"build","p":"Command line","u":"reference/cli.html#build","x":"python build.py build [-c site.yml] [--strict] Converts every page and writes the site to site_dir. The old output is replaced only after the new build succeeds. --strict makes the command exit with status 1 if there were warnings, such as a broken link, a missing include, or a nav entry that points at a missing file. Use it in CI."},{"t":"serve","p":"Command line","u":"reference/cli.html#serve","x":"python build.py serve [-c site.yml] [-p 8000] [--host 127.0.0.1] Builds the site, serves it locally, and rebuilds when anything in docs/, theme/ or site.yml changes. Open pages reload themselves."},{"t":"Warnings you may see","p":"Command line","u":"reference/cli.html#warnings-you-may-see","x":"Message Fix link to unknown page The .md file doesn't exist; check the path include not found Check the path, relative to the page or docs/ nav: page not found The file named in nav isn't under docs/ link target not found An image or file link points at a missing asset See configuration for the settings that affect the build."},{"t":"Introduction to System Simulation","p":"Introduction to System Simulation","u":"systemsimulation/systemsimulation.html","x":"Quick Quiz: What is the primary benefit of static site generators? Slower load times Blazing fast speed & high security Requires a heavy database Submit Answer function checkAnswer() { const selected = document.querySelector('input[name=\"q1\"]:checked'); const result = document.getElementById('quiz-result'); if (!selected) { result.style.color = \"orange\"; result.textContent = \"Please select an option first!\"; return; } if (selected.value === \"correct\") { result.style.color = \"green\"; result.textContent = \"Correct! Static sites don't rely on server-side databases.\"; } else { result.style.color = \"red\"; result.textContent = \"Incorrect. Try again!\"; } }"}];